# {{ name }}

A backend: a Django API for data no existing system holds, with its own web components that
any dashboard can show. Made from [Cooperation-org/baobab](https://github.com/Cooperation-org/baobab); its rules are
[CONTRACT.md](https://github.com/Cooperation-org/baobab/blob/main/CONTRACT.md).

`Item` in `api/models.py` and `<{{ slug }}-items>` are the example. Replace them with what this
backend owns and who may see it.

## Run it

```
uv venv && uv pip install -r requirements.txt
cp .env.example .env          # DATABASE_URL and the OIDC client
.venv/bin/python manage.py migrate
.venv/bin/python manage.py runserver 8001
.venv/bin/pytest
```

Production: `gunicorn config.wsgi:application`, after `manage.py collectstatic`.
Locally without an OIDC client: `manage.py createsuperuser`, sign in at `/admin/`.

## Sign-in (LinkedTrust)

1. Register a client, one per app. The LinkedTrust admin runs, in `trust_claim_backend`:
   ```
   npx ts-node scripts/register-oidc-client.ts --name "{{ name }}" \
     --redirect https://<this app's host>/auth/linkedtrust/callback
   ```
   Add a second `--redirect` for `http://localhost:8001/auth/linkedtrust/callback` to sign in locally.
2. Put the printed `client_id` and `client_secret` (shown once) in `.env` as
   `OIDC_CLIENT_ID` and `OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET`.

Endpoints, scopes and the flow: `trust_claim_backend/docs/sso-integration.md`.

## What it serves

| Path | What |
|---|---|
| `/auth/login/?next=` | Sign in, then back to `next` (a URL on an origin in `EMBED_ORIGINS`) |
| `/api/me/` | The signed-in person |
| `/api/items/` | GET the person's items (`?limit=`), POST one (`X-Embed: 1`) |
| `/static/embed/{{ slug }}.js` | The web components: `<{{ slug }}-items data-up="<this backend>" data-limit="5">` |

To show them on any dashboard, on the same registrable domain as this backend:

1. Put the dashboard's origin in `EMBED_ORIGINS` here.
2. On a dashboard made from the dashboard template: add this backend under Apps (API = this
   backend's URL, web components file = `<this backend>/static/embed/{{ slug }}.js`) and a
   card with `"app": "{{ slug }}", "tag": "{{ slug }}-items"`.
3. On any other page (GovKit's dash, a Django template, plain HTML):
   ```html
   <{{ slug }}-items data-up="https://<this backend>"></{{ slug }}-items>
   <script src="https://<this backend>/static/embed/{{ slug }}.js" defer></script>
   ```
   If that page sets a `Content-Security-Policy`, its `script-src` must allow this backend.

